From e4b2b39996e195a9e3c96939a6eded3cbcc0d4dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:33:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] decoder: decide stereo 3D video with the shared stereo
 policy

Whether a frame was 3D came from the stream's mark alone, and the halving of
a full side by side frame's display aspect ratio from two private numbers
(2.5 and 1.2). A video with no mark, such as a 3840x1080 MPEG-4 Part 2 AVI,
was never treated as 3D ("multiview 0"), so its pair was shown flat.

Ask libstereo-policy once per format change, in this order: the user's choice
(video-stereo-input, video-stereo-swap and the swap stored with the file), the
stream's own mark, the 3D tag of the file name, the frame's shape (side by
side from three times as wide as high, never top and bottom). Full or half
views come from the stream first (the Matroska plane size, kept by the
demuxer), then from the shape. The private numbers are gone. Without the
library the stream's mark is taken as it is.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
